From: PYNQ-Z2 board notes
Subject: [PATCH] usb: chipidea: host: drive external VBUS of a ULPI PHY

The Zynq-7000 USB controllers (CI_HDRC_PHY_VBUS_CONTROL) leave VBUS to the
PHY. On boards with a ULPI PHY such as the TUSB1210 and an external VBUS
switch on its CPEN pin, the PHY drives CPEN only if DrvVbusExternal is set
in its OTG Control register. With usb-nop-xceiv as the PHY, nothing sets
that bit, so VBUS stays off and no device is detected.

Set DrvVbus and DrvVbusExternal through the ULPI viewport when the port
power changes.

Tested on a TUL PYNQ-Z2 (TUSB1210, TPS2065 VBUS switch) with Linux 6.18.64.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/chipidea/host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/chipidea/host.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/string_choices.h>
 #include <linux/pinctrl/consumer.h>
+#include <linux/ulpi/regs.h>
 
 #include "../host/ehci.h"
 
@@ -68,6 +69,19 @@
 			usb_phy_vbus_on(ci->usb_phy);
 		else
 			usb_phy_vbus_off(ci->usb_phy);
+
+		/*
+		 * A ULPI PHY that switches VBUS with an external supply needs
+		 * DrvVbusExternal in its OTG Control register. A legacy PHY
+		 * such as usb-nop-xceiv does not set it, so set both VBUS bits
+		 * here through the ULPI viewport.
+		 */
+		if (ci->ulpi)
+			ci->ulpi_ops.write(ci->dev,
+					   enable ? ULPI_SET(ULPI_OTG_CTRL) :
+						    ULPI_CLR(ULPI_OTG_CTRL),
+					   ULPI_OTG_CTRL_DRVVBUS |
+					   ULPI_OTG_CTRL_DRVVBUS_EXT);
 	}
 
 	if (enable && (ci->platdata->phy_mode == USBPHY_INTERFACE_MODE_HSIC)) {
